# {{.Name}}

A Neutron Zig service. Requires **Zig 0.15.x** (0.15.2): the Neutron Zig SDK
does not compile on 0.16, which removed std APIs it uses.

## Getting started

```sh
{{range .NextSteps}}{{.}}
{{end}}```

`neutron dev` runs `zig build run` with the first Zig 0.15 it finds (`zig` on
PATH, then Homebrew's `zig@0.15`); the first build downloads the SDK. To build
without running, use `zig build` from a Zig 0.15.x.

The SDK is the `{{.SDK.Subdir}}/` directory of the Neutron repository, pinned to one
commit in `build.zig.zon` (the Zig package manager needs a content hash). To
move to a newer commit: `zig fetch --save=neutron <archive URL of that commit>`.

## Endpoints

- `GET /api/hello` — sample route in `src/main.zig`
- `GET /health` — `{"status", "nucleus", "version"}` via the SDK's `healthJson`

## Configuration

Read from the environment (`.env` lists them; nothing loads it automatically):

| Variable | Default |
|---|---|
| `NEUTRON_HOST` | `0.0.0.0` |
| `NEUTRON_PORT` | `8080` |
| `NEUTRON_DATABASE_URL` | unset — `/health` reports `"nucleus": "unconfigured"` |
| `NEUTRON_LOG_LEVEL` | `info` |
